silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_07_worked_household_to_vetclinic_sections_02_revised_functorial_transport_yoneda_hom_leg silm:hasExample "In 'RevisedFunctorialTransportYonedaHomLeg', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, the CSV is paired with the manifest. the transport functor F preserves this typed leg in the Mittens vet-clinic migration; the household-side arrow is named and the clinic-side image is named, with arrow direction and typing kept intact.; also, the clinic reconstructs KGvet via the typed arrows in the manifest" .
